To speed up the game, I collected many scrolls of magic mapping (about
12) before I got to Hell; asked for blessed spellbook of magic
mapping; weared +4 helm of brilliance to use the magic mapping spell
in the labyrinth.  This way I moved through the Gehennom very fast.

As always, I used to leave one food ration (or something similar) near
the ">" on each 3-rd level.  This lets me eat only regular food, not
corpses, when I go up with the Amulet - saves time when it is
precious.

At this game, all altars were non-coaligned (except one on Astral
Plane), and all altars without exception were with priest.  I was
lucky that I found holy water early at the game.



